<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's NLCF buys 10,000 tonnes of tapioca.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's NLCF buys 10,000 tonnes of tapioca.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's National Livestock Cooperatives Federation (NLCF) bought 10,000 tonnes of Thailand tapioca at $86.50 a tonne C&amp;F, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>They said it passed on tenders for 10,000 tonnes of copra due to higher offer prices.  </p>
<p>Traders said the NLCF bought the tapioca from Soon Hwa Seng for delivery by May 20 to the two South Korean ports of Inchon and Kunsan.</p>
<p>They said the premiums for ship rotation between the two ports were at $1.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
